### AutomorphicCongruences:L1/gu22-ordinary-hermitian-forms
Let K be an imaginary quadratic field in which p splits, G = G_2 = GU(2,2) the unitary similitude
group of the skew-Hermitian form w_2 = (0 1_2; −1_2 0) over O_K, and K′ ⊂ G(𝔸^p_f) a neat open
compact subgroup. On the ordinary locus of the integral model of the Shimura variety S_G(K′K_p)
(with its toroidal and minimal compactifications), and over its Igusa tower, define the space
V^q_{a,ord} (dual of the ordinary p-adic Hermitian modular forms; q = 0 for cusp forms, q = 1 for
all forms) of weight a with coefficients in Λ_2 = ℤ_p[[Γ_2]], Γ_2 = (1 + pℤ_p)^4 ⊂ T_2(ℤ_p), with
the q-expansions at the cusps x = diag(u, t ū^{-1}), the Hecke operators at unramified places, the
U_p-operators u_t for t = diag(p^{a_1},…,p^{a_4}), the ordinary projector e = lim u_t^{n!}, and the
universal ordinary cuspidal Hecke algebra h_{Σ,0}(K′; Λ). Specializations at arithmetic weights are
classical holomorphic Hermitian modular forms of weight (κ, κ; 0, 0)-type when the weight is
sufficiently regular. Write M^q=Hom_Λ(V^q,Λ) for the module of forms carrying q-expansions: V and M
are dual carriers and are not identified without a pairing.
Hypothesis: p splits in K; K′K_p neat; the p-adic weights are characters of T_2(ℤ_p) through Γ_2 and
µ_{p−1}^4.
Hypothesis: The Shimura variety, its compactifications, the automorphic bundles and the ordinary
Igusa tower are imported from AutomorphicPadicLFunctions:L4 (unitary PEL data) and
