### AutomorphicCongruences:L3/universal-deformation-ring-structure
Under FW Assumption 2.1 (L3/fw-residual-hypotheses), the universal deformation ring R_Σ(ρ̄) of ρ̄
unramified outside Σ is a flat O-algebra which is a complete intersection of Krull dimension 4 (FW
Prop. 2.4); there is a Zariski-dense open X^sm ⊂ Spec R_Σ(ρ̄) containing every point that is
ordinary up to twist (if ρ̄|_{G_{ℚ_p}} is reducible) or crystalline and short up to twist (if
irreducible), at which Spec R^χ_Σ(ρ̄) → Spec O is formally smooth, and R_Σ(ρ̄) is reduced (Cor.
2.5); the classical points (up to twist) are Zariski dense, so the surjection R_Σ(ρ̄) → 𝕋^Σ_{m_ρ̄}
is an isomorphism (Prop. 2.6); and there is a regular sequence (x_1, x_2, x_3) in 𝕋^Σ_{m_ρ̄} making
it a finite free module over Λ = O[[X_1, X_2, X_3]], such that classical points with the same image
in Spec Λ are all crystalline-short (resp. ordinary) up to twist or none are (Cor. 2.7). Finite
flatness over the regular ring Λ does not make R_Σ(ρ̄) regular; the main conjecture over R_Σ(ρ̄) is
formulated through perfect complexes and the regular subring Λ.
