triv_{z_Σ}: Δ_Σ(T_Σ) ↪ Frac Λ (Conj. 3.30's map). For every specialization λ: 𝕋 → R(𝔞) to a minimal
prime and every classical point λ_f: R(𝔞) → O_Iw there are commutative diagrams relating triv_{z_Σ},
triv_{z(𝔞)} and triv_{z(f)_Iw} (FW (1.2.2), (1.2.3), Props 3.22–3.23), and for Iwasawa-suitable λ
the same holds for the full fundamental lines with Euler factors. The Λ-valued map is obtained by
the determinant after restriction of scalars; it is the norm construction, not an identification
