### AutomorphicCongruences:L4/fw-pointwise-theorem
Let p ≥ 3 and f ∈ S_k(Γ_0(Np^r)) a normalized eigencuspform of weight k ≥ 2 whose residual
representation satisfies the hypotheses of FW Thm 5.1 (L3/fw-residual-hypotheses, T51), with the
auxiliary prime ℓ satisfying ℓ ∥ N. Then the zeta morphism gives an isomorphism triv_{z(f)_Iw}:
Δ_{O_Iw}(T(f)_Iw) ≅ O_Iw (FW Thm 5.1; Thm 1.7 is its narrower nontrivial-µ formulation);
equivalently char_{Λ_Iw}H²(ℤ[1/p], T ⊗ Λ_Iw) = char_{Λ_Iw}H¹(ℤ[1/p], T ⊗ Λ_Iw)/Λ_Iw·z(f)_Iw. This
covers non-ordinary and bad-reduction points at p (π(f)_p principal series, Steinberg or
supercuspidal) and needs no µ-invariant hypothesis. Consequences: Sel_ℚ(f) is finite iff L(f, k/2) ≠
0 (Cor. 5.3), and for an abelian variety of GL_2-type with L(A,1) ≠ 0 satisfying the hypotheses, the
p-part of the BSD formula holds (Cor. 5.4).
