formulation additionally requires µ nontrivial even in the reducible-at-p case.
Hypothesis: The scalar local semisimplification is automatically impossible: det ρ̄_f|I_p=ω^{k−1}
with k−1 odd; a scalar semisimplification would give ω^{2a} for some integer a, contradicting 2a≡k−1
mod p−1 because p is odd. Thus no additional scalar exclusion is missing from the displayed theorem
(FW p. 69).
Hypothesis: For the normalized residual representation in the proof on p. 73, the ramified Steinberg
witness also excludes quadratic-induced restriction exceptions: its nontrivial unipotent p-element
cannot occur in an induction from the index-two quadratic cyclotomic field, since ℓ≠p is unramified
there and prime-to-p characters have no such inertia image. Together with the local exclusion, this
supplies the A21/A35 dictionary; preserve the source’s critical twist.
Check: Exported to ModularIwasawaMainConjectures:L2/fw-pointwise-theorem in the cohomological (Kato)
form; the signed or ordinary scalar versions are the consumer's, after its separate local
comparison.
Source: FW-v3, Thm 5.1, p. 68; Thm 1.7, p. 7; Cors 5.3–5.4, p. 69; proof of Thm 5.1, p. 73.
Source: FW-v3, Remark after Thm 5.1, PDF p. 69; proof of Thm 5.1, p. 73.

